// The contributor registry — ONE record per person, joined from the three
// sources Banodoco publishes or generates about itself:
//
//   - ownership/data.js    the ledger mirror (who was granted, in which
//                          group, in which month, at what percentage)
//   - ownership/reasons.js the researched "what they actually did" line
//                          (generated by tools/build-reasons.js)
//   - the sprite table     this file's own PORTRAITS list — the avatar-tile
//                          coordinates from the published profile-sprite.jpg
//                          (banodoco.ai/profile-sprite.jpg), copied from the
//                          site's profilePicsManifest.ts
//
// `PERSON` is the canonical record: lowercase-keyed by username so any
// consumer can look anyone up without casing traps. Every page reads from
// PERSON — the home field deals from it (name/role/blurb/sprite), the
// ownership ledger renders from it (name/blurb/granted/total/months), and a
// future attribute (consent, socials, discord id) is one field in one place.
//
// WHY 120 SPRITE ROWS AND 370 PERSON ROWS. The sprite carries 198 avatars;
// these 120 are the ones whose username also matches a ledger row, so a face
// can be shown with a real name AND a real group. The remainder of PERSON is
// real contributors too — they simply have no published tile. Widening the
// sprite list is a name-normalisation exercise against the same two files,
// not new data.
//
// ROLE is the ledger group that person was granted in most often. The ledger's
// four groups are core, infrastructure builders, knowledge sharers and artists
// (banodoco.ai/ownership: 0.25% per group per month since February 2024), and
// the distribution below is theirs, not a design choice — artists are the
// largest group because they are.
//
// NO COUNTS (13-content-ops.md CO-3.1): grant frequency decided each person's
// role, but no tally is published here. A hand-maintained number goes stale;
// a group does not.

import { OWNERSHIP, GRANTS } from '../ownership/data.js';
import { REASONS } from '../ownership/reasons.js';

